John earns $25 per hour.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item He rents his car 10 times per month, and he rents it for 3 hours each time.
    \item So, the total rental hours are $10 \times 3 = 30$ hours.
    \item Therefore, the total earnings from renting the car are $30 \times 25 = $750$.
    \item His car payment is $500$.
    \item So, his profit is the earnings minus the car payment: $750 - 500 = $250$.
\end{enumerate}
Thus, John makes a profit of $250.

\boxed{250}

